    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d469">

                <pb facs="0799" n="1757" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1757"/>

                <head>No. 14.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Sir L. S. Sackville
                            West</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 11,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Complying with the request contained in
                    your note of the 8th instant, conveyed to me under the instructions of your
                    Government, I have the honor to inclose you two printed copies of the judicial
                    proceedings in the United States district court for the District of Alaska in
                    the several cases of libel against the schooners <hi rendition="#italic">Onward,
                        Carolena</hi>, and <hi rendition="#italic">Thornton</hi>, for killing fur
                    seals in Alaskan waters.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>




